{"text": "People show a tendency. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To trust ideas that correspond to their beliefs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Even though there is little or no objective evidence to support them. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Such ideas may eventually turn out to be false. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If the assumptions underlying them. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Largely rely on subjective observations. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Careful thinkers thus try to test their existing beliefs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Rather than simply maintaining them. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> When new evidence does not support the idea that they have entertained. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> They reexamine it. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> From alternative viewpoints. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This inspires them. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To go about challenging the problematic belief. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Therefore, thinking reflectively about the existing beliefs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Helps people adjust them. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> According to available evidence. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Furthermore, it enables people to become less likely to accept new ideas. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Just because they are tempting. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Or consistent with what they have long believed. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Although individuals differ considerably in their belief systems. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Those who objectify and test their own beliefs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Tend to think more critically. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Than those who do not.", "alignment": {"characters": ["P", "e", "o", "p", "l", "e", " ", "s", "h", "o", "w", " ", "a", " ", "t", "e", "n", "d", "e", "n", "c", "y", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "T", "o", " ", "t", "r", "u", "s", "t", " ", "i", "d", "e", "a", "s", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "c", "o", "r", "r", "e", "s", "p", "o", "n", "d", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", "i", "r", " ", "b", 